    you use a self-hosted deployment that you or your organization runs, that operator is responsible for the
    service and for its own terms. These Terms apply to the app and to the hosted service that we operate.
  </p>

  <h2 id="beta" data-toc-label="3. Beta software"><span class="legal-prose__num">03</span>Beta and pre-release software</h2>
  <div class="legal-note">
    <p>
      <strong>The Service is currently offered as a beta.</strong> It is provided for early evaluation and
      may contain bugs, incomplete features, and rough edges. Features may change, be added, or be removed at
      any time, and the Service may be interrupted or discontinued. We do not offer any uptime or service
      level commitment during the beta.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    You use the beta at your own risk. Do not rely on the beta as the sole store for information you cannot
    afford to lose, and keep your own backups of anything important. If you send us feedback, bug reports, or
    suggestions, you grant us a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to use them to improve the
    Service, without any obligation to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="eligibility" data-toc-label="4. Accounts"><span class="legal-prose__num">04</span>Eligibility and accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 16 years old to use the Service. If the law where you live sets a higher age of
    digital consent, you must meet that age. The Service is not directed to children.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for the accounts you create, for keeping your login credentials secure, and for all
    activity that happens under your account. Tell us promptly at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>
    {" "}if you believe your account has been accessed without your permission.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-service" data-toc-label="5. The Service"><span class="legal-prose__num">05</span>The Service</h2>
  <p>
    Uniffy is a unified workspace for notes, files, chat, projects, tasks, calendar, diagrams, rooms, and AI
    assistants, where content can be referenced from anywhere. Access to content is controlled by the
    permissions you set. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use the
    Service for your internal business or personal purposes, subject to these Terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may set reasonable technical limits, such as storage, request rate, or AI usage limits, and we may
    change them. We may release updates to the app and the hosted service from time to time.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use" data-toc-label="6. Acceptable use"><span class="legal-prose__num">06</span>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to, and not to allow anyone else to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the Service to break the law or to infringe the rights of others;</li>
    <li>upload or share content that is illegal, harmful, or that you have no right to share;</li>
    <li>attempt to access accounts, data, or systems that you are not authorized to access;</li>
    <li>interfere with, overload, or disrupt the Service, or bypass its security or usage limits;</li>
    <li>reverse engineer the hosted service except to the extent this restriction is prohibited by law;</li>
    <li>use the Service to send spam, malware, or to harass or abuse others.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
